{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01001",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.1,
      "end_seconds": 14.25,
      "duration_seconds": 13.15,
      "text": "The booking says \"tummy aches, sister has coeliac disease.\" Hi Ellis, I'm Dr Park. Mum, you're on the line too. Who wants to go first? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.23,
      "end_seconds": 28.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.35,
      "text": "Me, if that's okay. Ellis's older sister was diagnosed with coeliac disease in March, and since then I can't stop noticing how often Ellis complains about her stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.79,
      "end_seconds": 32.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "It's not that often. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.06,
      "end_seconds": 40.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Let's find out. Ellis, how long have the stomach aches been around?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.1,
      "end_seconds": 47.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Since the summer holidays. About three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 48.24,
      "end_seconds": 56.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Longer than that. It was Easter, I remember because she missed the egg hunt. That's eight months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.67,
      "end_seconds": 68.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.05,
      "text": "So somewhere between three and eight months. We don't need to settle it. What are they like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.24,
      "end_seconds": 75.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Like a crampy feeling, around my belly button, after lunch mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.99,
      "end_seconds": 80.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Anything else going on with your tummy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.39,
      "end_seconds": 89.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "I get bloated. My jeans feel tight even when I haven't eaten much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 91.0,
      "end_seconds": 97.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "And she's tired, she's always asleep on the sofa by seven."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.69,
      "end_seconds": 102.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I'm not always asleep. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.57,
      "end_seconds": 106.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "What about your poos?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.61,
      "end_seconds": 110.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Loose, sometimes. Pale. Gross."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.19,
      "end_seconds": 117.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Have you lost any weight that you know of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 119.99,
      "end_seconds": 125.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "No, if anything she's grown out of her shoes, so no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.64,
      "end_seconds": 131.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "What do you eat on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.37,
      "end_seconds": 142.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.04,
      "text": "Toast for breakfast, a pasta pot or a sandwich at lunch, and whatever mum cooks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 143.2,
      "end_seconds": 147.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Lots of bread and pasta, yes. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.66,
      "end_seconds": 152.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Right. Do you do any sport, Ellis?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.77,
      "end_seconds": 157.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Hockey, twice a week. I'm a defender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.86,
      "end_seconds": 161.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "And who's at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 164.05,
      "end_seconds": 167.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Me, my husband, Ellis and her sister."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.01,
      "end_seconds": 173.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Anything else in her medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 174.93,
      "end_seconds": 178.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Eczema when she was small."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.0,
      "end_seconds": 181.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 182.49,
      "end_seconds": 189.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Her adenoids out when she was four. And her appendix, two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.23,
      "end_seconds": 196.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "In the family, who else has coeliac disease or autoimmune things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 197.54,
      "end_seconds": 202.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Her sister, obviously. And my mother has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.04,
      "end_seconds": 206.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 207.42,
      "end_seconds": 217.66,
      "duration_seconds": 10.24,
      "text": "Possibly. After an antibiotic when she was about two she came out in a rash. I honestly don't know which one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.49,
      "end_seconds": 222.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "I don't remember."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.22,
      "end_seconds": 239.74,
      "duration_seconds": 15.52,
      "text": "I'll note a possible allergy, unconfirmed. Now, here's what I think. With a sister diagnosed, loose pale stools, bloating and tiredness, this could well be coeliac disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 240.93,
      "end_seconds": 245.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "So she should stop eating gluten? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.42,
      "end_seconds": 261.74,
      "duration_seconds": 15.32,
      "text": "Please don't, yet. If she stops, the blood test can come back falsely normal. Keep eating bread and pasta normally until the tests are done."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 263.52,
      "end_seconds": 268.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Good to know, I'd have started tomorrow. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.13,
      "end_seconds": 280.68,
      "duration_seconds": 10.55,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a coeliac antibody blood test, a total IgA level, a full blood count, and a ferritin level."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.27,
      "end_seconds": 286.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Do I need to fast? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.32,
      "end_seconds": 300.29,
      "duration_seconds": 12.97,
      "text": "No, eat normally. And I'd like to start ferrous sulfate, 200 mg, once a day, and vitamin D, 1000 units, once a day, in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 301.95,
      "end_seconds": 306.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Will the iron upset her tummy? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.63,
      "end_seconds": 311.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "It can. Take it with food. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 313.47,
      "end_seconds": 315.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    }
  ]
}
